      </th>
     <th><para unique="1045897">CPUID Feature Flag</para>
      </th>
     <th><para unique="1045899">Description</para>
      </th>
     </tr>
    </thead><tbody>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1046317">EVEX.LLIG.F3.0F.W0 78 /r</para>
      <para unique="1046318">VCVTTSS2USI r32, xmm1/m32{sae}</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046322">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046324">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046329">AVX512F</para>
      <para unique="1046333">OR AVX10.1<anchor id="+105922"/></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046335">Convert one single precision floating-point value from xmm1/m32 to one unsigned doubleword integer in r32 using truncation.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1046297">EVEX.LLIG.F3.0F.W1 78 /r</para>
      <para unique="1046298">VCVTTSS2USI r64, xmm1/m32{sae}</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046302">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046307">V/N.E.<footnote><para unique="1046306" format="TableFootnote">For this specific instruction, EVEX.W in non-64 bit is ignored; the instruction behaves as if the W0 version is used.</para>
        </footnote></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046312">AVX512F</para>
      <para unique="1046313">OR AVX10.1 <anchor id="+314235"/></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046315">Convert one single precision floating-point value from xmm1/m32 to one unsigned quadword integer in r64 using truncation.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    </tbody>
   </table>
  </encoding_table>
